  "issue_number": 2450,
  "issue_title": "feat(kraken): import deposits, withdrawals, staking/earn rewards via Ledgers API",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\nThe current Kraken sync only calls `TradesHistory`, which returns spot buy/sell trades. The Kraken [Ledgers API](https://docs.kraken.com/api/docs/rest-api/get-ledgers) \u2014 which covers **all other financial events** \u2014 is never called. Users with correctly-scoped API keys (Query Ledger Entries enabled) therefore see only token sells; deposits, withdrawals, staking rewards, Earn income, and standalone fees are silently absent.\n\n## What's missing\n\n| Event | Kraken API source | Currently synced |\n|---|---|---|\n| Spot buy / sell trades | `TradesHistory` | \u2713 |\n| Crypto deposit (external wallet \u2192 Kraken) | `Ledgers` type=`deposit` | \u2717 |\n| Fiat deposit (bank wire \u2192 Kraken) | `Ledgers` type=`deposit` | \u2717 |\n| Crypto withdrawal (Kraken \u2192 wallet) | `Ledgers` type=`withdrawal` | \u2717 |\n| Fiat withdrawal (Kraken \u2192 bank) | `Ledgers` type=`withdrawal` | \u2717 |\n| Staking reward | `Ledgers` type=`staking` | \u2717 |\n| Kraken Earn reward | `Ledgers` type=`earn` | \u2717 |\n| Standalone fee (not on a trade) | `Ledgers` type=`fee` | \u2717 |\n\nTypes intentionally skipped: `trade` (already covered by `TradesHistory`), `transfer` (internal Kraken sub-account movements), `margin`/`rollover`/`settled` (margin trading \u2014 deferred to follow-up).\n\n## Root cause\n\n`Provider::Kraken` has no `get_ledgers` method. `KrakenItem::Importer#fetch_trades` is the only transaction-level call. `KrakenAccount::Processor#process_trades` explicitly guards `return unless %w[buy sell].include?(type)` \u2014 anything else is dropped.\n\nThe user's API key **already requires** `Data \u2192 Query ledger entries` (no key change needed); the codebase simply never calls the endpoint.\n\n## Proposed implementation\n\n### 1. `Provider::Kraken` \u2014 add `get_ledgers`\n\n```ruby\ndef get_ledgers(start: nil, type: nil, offset: nil)\n  params = {}\n  params[\"start\"] = start.to_i.to_s if start.present?\n  params[\"type\"] = type.to_s if type.present?\n  params[\"ofs\"] = offset.to_i.to_s if offset.present?\n  private_post(\"Ledgers\", params)\nend\n```\n\nLedgers response shape:\n```json\n{\n  \"ledger\": {\n    \"LXXXXXX\": {\n      \"refid\": \"SXXXXXX\",\n      \"time\": 1609459200.123,\n      \"type\": \"withdrawal\",\n      \"subtype\": \"\",\n      \"aclass\": \"currency\",\n      \"asset\": \"XXBT\",\n      \"amount\": \"-0.10000000\",\n      \"fee\": \"0.00010000\",\n      \"balance\": \"0.40000000\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"count\": 2500\n}\n```\n\n`amount` is **net** (already accounts for the fee deducted from the sent amount). `fee` is the Kraken-charged portion, stored in `extra` for reference.\n\n### 2. `KrakenItem::Importer` \u2014 paginate and store ledgers\n\nSame loop as `fetch_trades` (max 200 pages \u00d7 50 entries). Result stored as:\n```ruby\nraw_transactions_payload: {\n  \"trades\"  => trades,\n  \"ledgers\" => ledgers   # new\n}\n```\n\n`type == \"trade\"` entries are **not filtered at fetch time** (store everything for auditability), but are skipped by the processor to avoid double-counting with `TradesHistory`.\n\n### 3. `KrakenAccount::LedgerProcessor` \u2014 new class\n\nCalled from `KrakenAccount::Processor#process` after `process_trades`. Iterates `raw_transactions_payload[\"ledgers\"]`, creates `Transaction` entries (not `Trade`) for each relevant event.\n\n**Dedup key:** `external_id: \"kraken_ledger_#{ledger_id}\"` \u2014 idempotent on re-sync.\n\n**Type \u2192 entry mapping:**\n\n| Ledger type | Entry amount sign | `investment_activity_label` | `kind` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `deposit` | positive (inflow) | `\"Contribution\"` | `funds_movement` |\n| `withdrawal` | negative (outflow) | `\"Withdrawal\"` | `funds_movement` |\n| `staking` | positive (income) | `\"Dividend\"` | `standard` |\n| `earn` | positive (income) | `\"Interest\"` | `standard` |\n| `fee` | negative (expense) | `\"Fee\"` | `standard` |\n| `trade` | \u2014 | skipped | |\n| `transfer` | \u2014 | skipped (internal) | |\n\n**Entry naming:** `\"Deposit 0.1 BTC\"`, `\"Staking reward 0.00123 ETH\"`, etc. \u2014 using normalized symbol via `AssetNormalizer`.\n\n### 4. Multi-currency amount resolution\n\nKraken `amount` is always in the native asset (e.g., BTC, EUR, USD, XRP). Resolution to family currency:\n\n1. Normalize raw asset code via `KrakenAccount::AssetNormalizer` \u2192 canonical symbol (XXBT\u2192BTC, ZUSD\u2192USD, ZEUR\u2192EUR)\n2. **If symbol == family currency** \u2192 use amount directly\n3. **If symbol is fiat (USD, EUR, GBP, CAD, AUD, CHF, JPY, AED)** \u2192 `ExchangeRate.find_or_fetch_rate(from: symbol, to: family_currency, date: entry_date)` (same mechanism as `KrakenAccount::UsdConverter`)\n4. **If symbol is crypto** \u2192 resolve via `KrakenAccount::SecurityResolver` + stored asset prices from `raw_payload[\"assets\"]` (already priced in USD by the importer's `ticker_price_for`), then convert USD\u2192family_currency via `UsdConverter`; if price is unavailable, set amount=0 and store `\"price_missing\": true` in `extra`\n\nThis is best-effort historical pricing using the importer's snapshot. A future enhancement could fetch OHLC at the entry date for higher accuracy.\n\n### 5. Stored metadata in `extra`\n\nEach ledger-derived entry gets:\n```json\n{\n  \"kraken\": {\n    \"ledger_id\": \"LXXXXXX\",\n    \"refid\": \"SXXXXXX\",\n    \"raw_asset\": \"XXBT\",\n    \"raw_amount\": \"-0.10000000\",\n    \"fee_native\": \"0.00010000\",\n    \"type\": \"withdrawal\",\n    \"subtype\": \"\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis preserves the original Kraken data for debugging and future reprocessing.\n\n## Files changed\n\n- `app/models/provider/kraken.rb` \u2014 `get_ledgers`\n- `app/models/kraken_item/importer.rb` \u2014 `fetch_ledgers`, pagination, store alongside trades\n- `app/models/kraken_account/ledger_processor.rb` \u2014 **new**\n- `app/models/kraken_account/processor.rb` \u2014 call `LedgerProcessor`\n- `test/models/provider/kraken_test.rb` \u2014 `get_ledgers` tests\n- `test/models/kraken_account/ledger_processor_test.rb` \u2014 **new**\n\n## Out of scope (follow-ups)\n\n- Extracting trade fees as separate line-item entries (currently embedded in the `Trade` record)\n- Margin trading: `margin`, `rollover`, `settled` ledger types\n- Kraken-to-Kraken sub-account transfers (`type=transfer`)\n- OHLC-based historical pricing for crypto ledger amounts",
  "merged_at": "2026-06-30T05:35:14.000Z",
